.TH WALLPAPER-SUITE 1 "October 2026" "Wallpaper Suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wallpaper-suite \- open the per-monitor wallpaper manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wallpaper-suite
.RB [ --migrate-only ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open Wallpaper Suite preferences in a GNOME desktop session.
When GNOME cannot open preferences, show an actionable error window.
.PP
The original unmodified user-installed app shortcut is moved into the
wallpaper-suite/launcher-backups directory under the user's XDG state directory.
This lets the current packaged shortcut take precedence.
Customized shortcuts and symbolic links are preserved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --migrate-only
Check and migrate the original shortcut without opening preferences.
The Debian package runs this check at GNOME login.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, one on a launch or migration failure, and 64 for invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wallpaper-suitectl (1),
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
